.LONG TERM...
Issued at 1232 PM PDT Tue Sep 22 2026
(Thursday through next Monday)

Thursday looks to be the warmest across the interior with similar
temperatures to Wednesday elsewhere. On Friday, a developing trough
off of the West Coast will return resulting in a cooling trend and
deepening of the marine layer. The coolest conditions are expected
Saturday and Sunday as a reinforcing trough deepens off of the
California coast with temperatures up to 10-15 deg F below
seasonal averages. Temperatures appear to rebound closer to normal
for this time of year early next week as the trough flattens and
the 500 mb height clusters point to a building ridge over the
western United States.

