.AVIATION...
(18Z TAFS)
Issued at 1107 AM PDT Tue Sep 22 2026

MVFR to IFR ceilings associated with the marine layer will gradually
scatter out in the next couple of hours, resulting in widespread VFR
conditions at most terminals. Low confidence on whether HAF will see
the sun as there may be a brief period of scattered clouds before
becoming BKN again. The usual diurnal onshore wind pattern prevails
through the afternoon with a light south to southwest flow overnight
across our region. The marine layer will compress overnight. Exactly
how much is uncertain. Moderate confidence for STS, LVK, SJC, and
SFO to remain VFR through the TAF cycle with advertised SCT decks
early Wednesday morning. There is a 60-70% chance for APC and OAK to
develop BKN ceilings given their exposed locations, though it may be
intermittent depending on the marine layer depth tonight.

Vicinity of SFO...VFR prevails this afternoon with low to medium
confidence on the return of MVFR ceilings tonight. Should ceilings
develop, they will likely roll in around the time of the SCT decks
as advertised. OAK has a higher probability of developing MVFR
ceilings early Wednesday morning compared to SFO. Westerly winds
increase to moderate this afternoon and ease to a light
southwesterly flow Wednesday morning before increasing again.

SFO Bridge Approach...Current satellite imagery shows a final push
of stratus across the bridge, but should become VFR in the next hour
or so. Patchy cloud cover is possible over the eastern side of the
bridge tonight. Otherwise, similar to SFO.

Monterey Bay Terminals...Borderline MVFR-IFR ceilings linger through
the next couple of hours with a brief period of VFR conditions.
Medium to high confidence for an early onset of IFR ceilings around
4-7 PM PDT impacting MRY first and then SNS. Low confidence on
whether ceilings will drop to LIFR territory early Wednesday
morning. For now, the TAF advertises borderline IFR-LIFR with slight
impacts to visibility due to mist and/or drizzle. Onshore winds
increase to 7-10 kt this afternoon and gradually become light
southerly breezes overnight.

